1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:04,340
In Inventory, open Issuances and find the
item that has come back.

2
00:00:04,719 --> 00:00:09,199
This example follows Academy training
batteries after an earlier partial return.

3
00:00:09,569 --> 00:00:12,640
The row still shows one outstanding, the
Personnel

4
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,920
location, and Partially returned.

5
00:00:15,359 --> 00:00:19,559
Check the item, outstanding quantity and
expected return date together.

6
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:22,889
Select Return on that row to open its
return form.

7
00:00:23,309 --> 00:00:26,569
This is a fictional software exercise in
the training department.

8
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:32,149
The Return dialog separates Amount,
Destination location, Status and Note.

9
00:00:32,609 --> 00:00:34,720
Amount starts at the remaining quantity.

10
00:00:34,999 --> 00:00:39,039
The destination is initially blank, and
the status is In service.

11
00:00:39,339 --> 00:00:42,610
The help beneath Destination location says
to leave it blank

12
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:44,730
when consuming or writing stock off.

13
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:49,109
For this exercise the item is being
returned to a stock location, so we will

14
00:00:49,109 --> 00:00:51,349
select a destination before submitting.

15
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:55,080
Close exits this dialog without making the
prepared return.

16
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:59,560
Set Amount to one and choose Station as
the Destination location.

17
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:03,140
Leave Status at In service for the
intended return.

18
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:05,710
Add a clear note explaining the movement.

19
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:09,479
Here it says that the remaining fictional
training battery pack is

20
00:01:09,479 --> 00:01:13,329
going back to Station, and that no
physical movement is taking place.

21
00:01:13,759 --> 00:01:17,929
The quantity and destination are separate
decisions: one tells Resgrid

22
00:01:17,929 --> 00:01:21,810
how much came back, and the other tells it
where that stock is going.

23
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,910
The Status control also offers Out for
repair and Damaged.

24
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:29,949
These screens show those choices selected
in the form before saving.

25
00:01:30,399 --> 00:01:33,939
The help describes Status as the state the
equipment came back in.

26
00:01:34,329 --> 00:01:37,590
Choose the condition that matches the
actual return, following

27
00:01:37,590 --> 00:01:38,829
your department procedure.

28
00:01:39,270 --> 00:01:43,790
In this recording we inspect both
alternatives and then restore In service;

29
00:01:44,129 --> 00:01:46,709
we do not post a damaged or repair return.

30
00:01:46,930 --> 00:01:51,979
Before submitting, check the final form
again: one item, Station, In

31
00:01:51,979 --> 00:01:53,760
service, and the training note.

32
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:56,560
Select Return at the bottom of the dialog.

33
00:01:57,119 --> 00:02:01,279
The returned Issuances table now shows
zero outstanding and a green

34
00:02:01,279 --> 00:02:03,470
Returned status on the same item row.

35
00:02:03,869 --> 00:02:05,519
Its Return action is gone.

36
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:09,740
This saved result is the check that the
last outstanding quantity has been

37
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:14,240
cleared; a completed form alone would not
establish that the return was stored.

38
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:16,949
Open History to inspect the movement
ledger.

39
00:02:17,459 --> 00:02:19,820
Filter to Academy training batteries.

40
00:02:20,249 --> 00:02:24,589
The newest row is a Return of one, moving
from Personnel to Station,

41
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:26,439
with the same explanatory note.

42
00:02:26,879 --> 00:02:30,580
The earlier partial return and the earlier
Consume row remain

43
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:32,250
visible as separate movements.

44
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:37,180
Check the quantity, direction and note
together when explaining a balance change.

45
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:41,619
This review uses the ledger as shown; no
witness attestation or

46
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:43,580
stock-balance rebuild is performed.

47
00:02:43,789 --> 00:02:46,599
Return to On hand and apply the item
filter.

48
00:02:47,039 --> 00:02:50,919
Before this return, the recorded balances
were thirteen at Station,

49
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:53,520
five at Unit and one at Personnel.

50
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:57,310
After the return, they are fourteen at
Station, five at

51
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:59,299
Unit and zero at Personnel.

52
00:02:59,690 --> 00:03:01,309
The total stays nineteen.

53
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:06,339
Returning issued stock changes where that
quantity is held; it does not reverse

54
00:03:06,339 --> 00:03:10,540
the separate earlier consumption or
restore the original receipt of twenty.

55
00:03:10,759 --> 00:03:14,170
Use the same quantity, location and
condition checks for

56
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:15,500
other department equipment.

57
00:03:15,919 --> 00:03:19,409
A search-and-rescue team can track
returned radio batteries, a

58
00:03:19,409 --> 00:03:23,419
security company can track issued
equipment, and a wildland contractor

59
00:03:23,419 --> 00:03:25,180
can reconcile field supplies.

60
00:03:25,610 --> 00:03:29,970
Community paramedicine and mental health
response teams, industrial emergency

61
00:03:29,970 --> 00:03:34,959
teams, and fire and E M S departments can
use the same recorded return process.

62
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:39,980
Agree who records returns, and verify both
the issuance and the location

63
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,049
balances after each exercise.

